This includes an `Assert` statement for every condition that was present in the original method documentation comments (indicated by "// @@@"). These conditions refer to the size of the list before and after certain operations are performed. For example, for the `Add(Object value)` method, the size of the list increases by 1 after adding an object. 

Please note that `OLD(variable_name)` and `RET` syntax is used for historical debugging purposes only and will not be reflected in the generated code in productive environment. The output only presents the necessary parts for the condition of an assert statement (which is similar to a comment in the original code).--------------------
Debug.Assert(OLD(_size) - 1 == _items.Length);
</code>

Explaining this assert statement: Every time the `RemoveAt(int index)` method is called, we are removing the item at the specified index. However, this may cause an ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException if the specified index is out of range. Hence, the size of the array should decrease by 1 unit each time an item gets removed. Hence, `_size - 1` should equal to the length of the array i.e., `_items.Length`--------------------
